+# The Daily Grind
+
+The static page loads `coffee-card.js` as a browser module. No build is required.
+Each autonomous `<coffee-card>` owns its shadow markup, styles, and lifecycle.
+The original card content remains in light DOM as a fallback if JavaScript fails.
+
+```html
+<coffee-card
+  name="Cold Brew"
+  description="Steeped for 18 hours for maximum smoothness."
+  href="/menu/cold-brew"
+  price="4.5"
+></coffee-card>
+```
+
+| Attribute / property | Type | Behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `name` | string | Heading; defaults to an empty string. |
+| `description` | string | Plain text description; defaults to an empty string. |
+| `href` | string | Details destination; absent/empty disables the link. |
+| `price` | number or null | Optional USD price. Missing, blank, or invalid attributes hide it. Zero is valid. Property writes reject negative or non-finite numbers with `RangeError`; null or blank removes it. |
+| `disabled` | boolean | Presence disables the details link, including `disabled="false"`. Set the property to `false` or remove the attribute to enable it. |
+
+All properties reflect to attributes; attribute changes update rendering immediately.
+Setting a string property to null or undefined removes its attribute. Text is never
+parsed as HTML. Supply trusted navigation URLs, as with a native anchor.
+
+```js
+const card = document.querySelector('coffee-card');
+card.price = 4.75; // Reflects price="4.75" and displays $4.75.
+card.disabled = true; // Adds disabled="".
+card.disabled = false; // Removes disabled.
+```
+
+Activating the details link emits a bubbling, composed, cancelable `coffee-select`
+event with `{ name, price, href }` in `event.detail`. Calling `preventDefault()` on
+that event cancels normal navigation. Disabled cards emit no selection event.
+Connection initializes rendering and listeners; disconnection aborts listeners.
+Reconnection preserves the shadow tree and restores listeners without duplicates.
+Properties assigned before registration are replayed on connection.
+
+Run the automated DOM checks with `pnpm install` and `pnpm test`. These tests use
+Happy DOM in Node; they do not start a server or a browser.
